ion","level":"Medium","text":"Acquisitions, internal investment, debt, dividends, and repurchases can create or destroy per-share value.","signal":"Return on invested capital, impairments, leverage, share count, and post-investment cash generation"},{"title":"Reporting, legal, and governance","level":"Medium","text":"Controls, estimates, litigation, tax, incentives, or governance choices can alter reported economics and owner outcomes.","signal":"Restatements, control weaknesses, estimate changes, proceedings, proxy incentives, and related-party disclosures"}],"monitor":[{"title":"Latest 10-Q versus prior expectations","text":"Compare reported operating drivers, cash conversion, balance-sheet changes, and risk language with the prior quarter and owner thesis.","impact":"NEUTRAL"},{"title":"Management commentary versus delivery","text":"Record the measurable commitments made in the latest official earnings materials and test them against subsequent filings.","impact":"BULL CASE"},{"title":"Downside leading indicators","text":"Watch Transactions, bookings, cancellations, markdowns, and satisfaction; Market share, acquisition cost, incentives, take rate, and retention; Turns, utilization, residual values, losses, and fixed obligations.","impact":"BEAR CASE"},{"title":"Per-share capital allocation","text":"Measure whether retained cash, acquisitions, debt reduction, dividends, and repurchases improve durable value per diluted share.","impact":"NEUTRAL"}],"questions":["Which disclosed operating metric best proves that DARDEN RESTAURANTS INC is strengthening its position in company-operated restaurant brands, menu innovation, loyalty, digital ordering, franchising, and restaurant-level economics?","What changed in the latest 10-Q relative to the preceding 10-K and management''s prior commentary?","Which portion of reported growth is recurring, contractual, or repeatable, and which portion is cyclical or one-time?","What balance-sheet or off-balance-sheet obligation matter